Package: zcurve3
Type: Package
Title: Estimating Power, Publication Bias, and Effect-Size Heterogeneity from Significant Test Statistics
Version: 3.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ulrich", "Schimmack", email = "ulrich.schimmack@utoronto.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(c("František"), "Bartoš", role = "aut"),
    person("Jerry", "Brunner", role = "aut"))
Description: Fits a flexible, distribution-free mixture model to the significant
    z-values reported in a literature and returns the discovery, replication,
    and false-discovery rates implied by the observed distribution of evidence
    (expected discovery rate, expected replication rate, false-discovery rate).
    When effect sizes are supplied it additionally estimates the effect-size
    distribution behind the significant results, including per-study
    shrinkage-adjusted effects and heterogeneity, and draws a minimum-effect
    forest plot. Extends the 'zcurve' (z-curve 2.0) approach with effect-size
    estimation, directional and clustered analyses, and a rewritten plot.
